{{!
    @template block_dash/add_block_button

    Dash's "Add a block" button of a block region, opening a chooser with the blocks and the Dash
    gallery. Same markup as core/add_block_button, so themes and Behat steps treat it alike.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * link - URL of core's page for adding a block.
    * escapedlink - The same URL's query string, for adding blocks from the chooser.
    * pagehash - Hash of the edited page.
    * blockregion - Region the block is added to.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "link": "/my/index.php?bui_addblock&bui_blockregion=content&sesskey=M3mes",
        "escapedlink": "?bui_addblock&bui_blockregion=content&sesskey=M3mes",
        "pagehash": "abcdefgh",
        "blockregion": "side-pre"
    }
}}
<div class="d-grid" data-region="add-block-button">
    <a href="{{link}}" id="addblock-{{uniqid}}" class="btn btn-add-content mb-3" data-key="addblock" data-action="block_dash-addblock"
            data-url="{{escapedlink}}" data-blockregion="{{blockregion}}" data-pagehash="{{pagehash}}">
        <i class="fa fa-plus py-2 me-2" aria-hidden="true"></i>{{#str}}addblock{{/str}}
    </a>
</div>
{{#js}}
    require(['block_dash/add_block'], function(addBlock) {
        addBlock.init();
    });
{{/js}}
